                    {
                        "sense_id": "7db4421d-180f-37ca-8d01-79e54eb40c54",
                        "entry_id": "e87a8361-ab4a-39c0-a4ed-b9826dc7a3ab",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A divine mystery; something known only to God, or revealed only in holy scriptures."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "obsolete",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4f603f05-76d5-4af6-aca5-bb59eb0f226a",
                                "sense_id": "7db4421d-180f-37ca-8d01-79e54eb40c54",
                                "text": "But yet there is a place that men clepe the school of God, where he was wont to teach his disciples, and told them the privities of heaven."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "50dca84a-1590-3174-9af4-b2f35dd8ae7f",
                        "entry_id": "e87a8361-ab4a-39c0-a4ed-b9826dc7a3ab",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Privacy, secrecy."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "archaic",
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a9419bb0-343c-4841-8f79-5f3a79294df0",
                                "sense_id": "50dca84a-1590-3174-9af4-b2f35dd8ae7f",
                                "text": "Him oft and oft I askt in priuitie, / Of what loines and what lignage I did spring[…]."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3412db11-6836-3d72-95c5-3f06cae5e2c3",
                        "entry_id": "e87a8361-ab4a-39c0-a4ed-b9826dc7a3ab",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A private matter, a secret."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "obsolete",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "957305eb-8427-397a-aeb4-fca3427e7152",
                        "entry_id": "e87a8361-ab4a-39c0-a4ed-b9826dc7a3ab",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The genitals."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "archaic",
                            "countable",
                            "in-plural",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0bc98078-0742-4447-bb47-75cf920684ec",
                                "sense_id": "957305eb-8427-397a-aeb4-fca3427e7152",
                                "text": "Having ended the delights of nature, they were wont to wipe their privities [translating catze] with perfumed wooll."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a65f8195-f9a1-3788-9bf8-c437cff20635",
                        "entry_id": "e87a8361-ab4a-39c0-a4ed-b9826dc7a3ab",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A relationship between parties seen as being a result of their mutual interest or participation in a given transaction, e.g. contract, estate, etc."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "fbe49762-7924-4d7f-afe8-aff4554780bb",
                                "sense_id": "a65f8195-f9a1-3788-9bf8-c437cff20635",
                                "text": "There is no privity, (as the lawyers say),—that is, no mutual recognition, consent and agreement—between those who take these oaths, and any other persons."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d6306d90-d25c-3d49-9177-231e1bc64413",
                        "entry_id": "e87a8361-ab4a-39c0-a4ed-b9826dc7a3ab",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The fact of being privy to something; knowledge, compliance."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "94bfe437-25c2-4a8e-b406-d153746d7f18",
                                "sense_id": "d6306d90-d25c-3d49-9177-231e1bc64413",
                                "text": "But this acknowledgement was made without the privity of his wife, whose vicious aversion he was obliged, in appearance, to adopt."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "601de6d9-2286-4a70-8e8d-422f5a16b582",
                                "sense_id": "d6306d90-d25c-3d49-9177-231e1bc64413",
                                "text": "This episode in her life, above all other things, was most cruelly suggestive to him, as possibly involving his father in the privity to a thing, at which Pierre’s inmost soul fainted with amazement and abhorrence."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
